      <div type="clause" n="7">
        <head>App AGu 7</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="App AGu 7" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="395" ed="#liebermann"/>Et qui furem dimittet.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#App-AGu_7.lnote.oe.12"/> uel ad capiendum eum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#App-AGu_7.lnote.oe.13"/> adiuuare<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#App-AGu_7.lnote.oe.14"/> dissimulabit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#App-AGu_7.lnote.oe.star2"/>, emendet sicut supra dictum est.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="395" ed="#liebermann"/>7. Und wer einen Dieb entkommen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#App-AGu_7.lnote.de.1"/> lässt oder zaudert zu helfen ihn zu fassen, büsse wie oben [c. 6, 1] gesagt ist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">7. And whoever lets a thief escape or hesitates to help to seize him, let him pay compensation as is said above [c. 6, 1].</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann"/>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">*III Em. 2</note>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text and German translation transcribed from Gesetze I p. 395 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page); Liebermann’s print has a stray full stop in ‘dimittet.’; transcribed as printed</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="App-AGu_7.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">395</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">für</hi> wandie <hi rend="italic">I Ew Pr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">for wandie I Ew Pr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="App-AGu_7.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">395</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-tat <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-tat MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="App-AGu_7.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">395</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="App-AGu_7.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">395</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">iuuare <hi rend="italic">TMHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">iuuare TMHkBr</seg></note>
